Apache Tomcat is a web server and Servlet container.
It is mainly used to run Java web applications.
Tomcat supports technologies like Servlets and JSP.
Java web applications are commonly packaged as WAR files.
Tomcat deploys and runs these WAR applications.
Its default HTTP port is usually 8080.
The webapps folder is commonly used to deploy applications.
Tomcat can be started and stopped using its startup/shutdown scripts.
Jenkins can build a Java application and deploy it to Tomcat.
Tomcat helps developers host and run Java web application
